    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\npairs\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be nice to have [endwise](https://github.com/tpope/vim-endwise/blob/master/plugin/endwise.vim)-like functionality, either as a new module or as a part of `pairs`. It gets annoying to type `end` when editing Lua and tpope's plugin doesn't cooperate well with other plugins that map `<cr>` in insert mode.\r\n\r\nI could try to implement it. Looking at tpope's code, it's not that complex.",
