        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski; mind sharing how you use snippets for this? i'm assuming a snippet that fills out the `if thing then..end` block; if so, then yes this is great, but there are still cases where, for instance, in lua at least, `do<CR>` is faster (also am making assumptions about how one might have their completion plugin of choice setup).\r\n\r\nBasically, these steps:\r\n- Install snippet plugin. At the moment I use [L3MON4D3/LuaSnip](https://github.com/L3MON4D3/LuaSnip) (until possible future 'mini.snippets' :) ).\r\n- Define/install snippets you want to use. [rafamadriz/friendly-snippets](https://github.com/rafamadriz/friendly-snippets) is a great start. I prefer having all my snippets [manually defined](https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/tree/master/misc/snippets).\r\n- Use snippet engine. Either with completion plugin like [hrsh7th/nvim-cmp](https://github.com/hrsh7th/nvim-cmp) ('mini.completion' doesn't handle snippets by design; at least at the moment) or by manually triggering when you know the snippet should expand. I use a [somewhat hacky approach](https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/blob/master/lua/ec/configs/luasnip.lua) to get notification if snippet can be expanded, which is more than enough for me.",
            "created_at": "2022-11-10T08:02:23Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/9#issuecomment-1309909657",
